foundation.question_text:
A projectile launched from the origin follows $y=\dfrac{4}{3}x-\dfrac{1}{72}x^{2}$, where $x$ and $y$ are in metres. The point $P$ on the path is shown below. Find the direction of motion at $P$, where $x=60$, to 1 d.p.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$ (m)}, ylabel={$y$ (m)}, xmin=-10, xmax=112, ymin=-5, ymax=40, width=10cm, height=7cm, samples=100, clip=false, xtick={0,20,40,60,80,100}, ytick={0,10,20,30}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:96] {4*x/3 - x*x/72};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(60,30)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:60,30) {$P$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
$\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\dfrac{4}{3}-\dfrac{x}{36}$
At $x=60$, $\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\dfrac{4}{3}-\dfrac{60}{36}$
$=-\dfrac{1}{3}$
$\phi=\tan^{-1}\left(\dfrac{1}{3}\right)$
$\approx 18.4^{\circ}$ below the horizontal
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$ (m)}, ylabel={$y$ (m)}, xmin=-10, xmax=112, ymin=-5, ymax=40, width=10cm, height=7cm, samples=100, clip=false, xtick={0,20,40,60,80,100}, ytick={0,10,20,30}]
\addplot[thick, domain=0:96] {4*x/3 - x*x/72};
\addplot[dashed, domain=45:80] {30 - (x-60)/3} node[pos=1, right] {tangent at $P$};
\addplot[only marks, mark=*] coordinates {(60,30)};
\node[above right] at (axis cs:60,30) {$P$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

